# Drafted by Gemini (R25 endings), edited.

~ start
Narrator: You turned your backs upon the blazing ridge of Rowan's Rise, leaving the chant on the moor to reach its final, dreadful measure.
Narrator: Woven from dry timber and old malice, the Wicker Man steps down from the high heather with furnace fire roaring in his ribs.
Narrator: Each heavy stride shakes the valley floor as the giant walks toward the lanterns of Wickermoor Village.
Narrator: Roofs catch like dry straw before him, and the ancient bark of the Oak of Many Faces blackens and splits in the blinding heat.
Narrator: By the time the clocktower falls silent, only grey cinders drift across the Founder's Round like warm winter snow.
the_vagrant [sad]: The old prophecy came due ahead of time, and it left nothing in the hollow but soot and quiet.
Narrator: You watch from the far hills as the last sparks die into the heather, leaving the valley dark and empty under the moon.
-> END
